<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Conclusion Program:</strong> The day concluded with a closing program, marking the end of a memorable experience for all participants. Guests who attended the conclusion program expressed their appreciation for the initiative, proudly acknowledging the positive impact it had on the children. They were deeply moved by the love and care shown by Coastal Friends and were proud of the initiative.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At the conclusion program, the event was graced by several esteemed guests who played a significant role in making it a grand success. The list of dignitaries included <strong>Nasir Lucky Star</strong> (Waqf Chairman DK, Govt of Karnataka), <strong>Hasir Marine</strong> (Partner, Marine), <strong>Raheem Expertise</strong> (Director of Expertise), <strong>Arjun Bhandarkar</strong> (President of Save Life Charitable Trust), <strong>Saiduddin</strong> (Vice President of Talent Research Foundation), <strong>Mahammad Ali Kammaradi</strong> (Ex-member, Food Commission, Govt of Karnataka), <strong>Shahul Hameed KK</strong> (President of Minority Cell, DK Congress), <strong>Shabeer Siddakatte</strong> (General Secretary of Minority, DK Congress), <strong>Latheef Gurupura</strong> (MD of Ani Trading), <strong>Siraj Parladka</strong> (Founder of Coastal Friends Mangalore), and <strong>Shareef Abbas Valal</strong> (President of Coastal Friends Mangalore). Their presence added immense value to the event, and their support was greatly appreciated by the entire Coastal Friends team.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Throughout the day, Coastal Friends Mangalore members treated the children with love, care, and attention, as though they were their own. The children were embraced with warmth and affection, enjoying every moment alongside the volunteers. The bond between the children and the volunteers grew stronger, filled with smiles, laughter, and lasting memories.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">As a token of appreciation, <strong>Rs. 10,000 worth hampers</strong> were given to each child who participated, ensuring they left with a special gift.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The event was also supported by a dedicated medical team and comprehensive transportation facilities, ensuring the safety and well-being of all participants.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In addition, Coastal Friends Mangalore made a generous contribution to the community by donating <strong>50 wheelchairs</strong> to individuals in need, ensuring that those who required mobility support could benefit from the donation.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The <strong>positive message</strong> of the event, as conveyed by Coastal Friends Founder Mr. Siraj Parladka, was powerful: <em>&#8220;They are not orphans; they are our special guests.&#8221;</em> This message reflected the core belief that these children are not to be pitied, but celebrated as valuable members of the community.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The event was proudly called <strong>&#8220;A Blessed Day with Our Kids – Happiest Moments of Our Life&#8221;</strong>, encapsulating the joy, love, and unforgettable memories created throughout the day.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Coastal Friends Mangalore extends its heartfelt gratitude to all those who supported and contributed to the success of this event. Special thanks to the <strong>Police team, media, the public, guests, resort officials, Pilikula officials</strong>, and <strong>public personalities</strong> who joined our poster campaign. We are also thankful to the <strong>actors, politicians, social media influencers</strong>, and most importantly, the <strong>parents of the children</strong>, for their support and trust. Their presence and involvement helped make this event a truly memorable and impactful experience.</p>



